From f463df55d56581b72b3b614bb97313c99b6d76b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:20:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] package.json: the web/ modules are ESM

web/fm1pkg.js and web/fm1ota.js are ES modules, and the Node tests import them from .mjs. Without a
package.json Node guesses a .js file's type, and an ambient one above the checkout ("type":
"commonjs") makes the installer-boot test fail on a module it cannot find a named export in. Say
it here: the tree's JavaScript is ESM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 package.json | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package.json

diff --git a/package.json b/package.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0e9e778
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package.json
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+{
+  "name": "fm1-base",
+  "private": true,
+  "type": "module"
+}
-- 
2.55.0

